@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] smtp-local-service-boundary
SMTP and metrics MUST bind only to literal IPv4 loopback without opening firewall
ports. Only the relay may receive its upstream credentials through systemd;
Marshall receives local transport settings, not provider credentials. Upstream
TLS and authentication MUST remain mandatory.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:deployment] smtp-shared-launch-settings
Serving and migration launchers MUST use the same module-owned mail transport,
sender and port in relay mode, overriding conflicting environment-file settings.
Direct SMTP deployments MUST retain their previous configuration when disabled.
